# Unit03
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit03核心词汇

clash/klæʃ/冲突/The two groups clashed over the issue.
classic/ˈklæsɪk/经典的/This novel is a classic of English literature.
clause/klɔːz/条款；从句/Please check the contract clause carefully.
client/ˈklaɪənt/客户/The lawyer met with his client this morning.
climate/ˈklaɪmət/气候/Climate change is a global concern.
cling/klɪŋ/紧抓/She clung to her mother's hand.
coincidence/koʊˈɪnsɪdəns/巧合/It was a coincidence that we met there.
collapse/kəˈlæps/倒塌；崩溃/The old building collapsed in the earthquake.
colleague/ˈkɑːliːɡ/同事/She gets along well with her colleagues.
colonial/kəˈloʊniəl/殖民的/The country has a colonial history.
combine/kəmˈbaɪn/结合/We should combine theory with practice.
command/kəˈmænd/命令/He commanded the soldiers to stand down.
comment/ˈkɑːment/评论/She made a comment about the new policy.
commission/kəˈmɪʃn/委员会；佣金/He receives a 10% commission on each sale.
commit/kəˈmɪt/犯；承诺/He committed a serious error in judgment.
commodity/kəˈmɑːdəti/商品/Oil is an important commodity in global trade.
communicate/kəˈmjuːnɪkeɪt/交流/It's important to communicate clearly.
community/kəˈmjuːnəti/社区/The local community organized a festival.
compact/kəmˈpækt/紧凑的/This compact car is easy to park.
companion/kəmˈpæniən/同伴/The dog is a faithful companion.
comparable/ˈkɑːmpərəbl/可比较的/The two products are comparable in quality.
comparison/kəmˈpærɪsn/比较/There is no comparison between the two.
compassion/kəmˈpæʃn/同情/She showed compassion for the poor.
compatible/kəmˈpætəbl/兼容的/These two devices are not compatible.
compel/kəmˈpel/强迫/The evidence compelled him to change his mind.
compensate/ˈkɑːmpenseɪt/补偿/The company compensated the workers for their loss.
competent/ˈkɑːmpɪtənt/有能力的/She is a competent and experienced manager.
compile/kəmˈpaɪl/编纂/She compiled a list of useful references.
complement/ˈkɑːmplɪment/补充/The two approaches complement each other.
complex/ˈkɑːmpleks/复杂的/The issue is more complex than we thought.
complicated/ˈkɑːmplɪkeɪtɪd/复杂的/The instructions are too complicated to follow.
component/kəmˈpoʊnənt/组成部分/Quality is a key component of the product.
compose/kəmˈpoʊz/组成；创作/The team is composed of experts from various fields.
comprehensive/ˌkɑːmprɪˈhensɪv/全面的/We need a comprehensive review of the policy.
compromise/ˈkɑːmprəmaɪz/妥协/They reached a compromise after long negotiations.
compulsory/kəmˈpʌlsəri/必修的；强制的/English is a compulsory subject in schools.
conceal/kənˈsiːl/隐藏/He tried to conceal his true feelings.
conceive/kənˈsiːv/构想/She conceived a plan to solve the problem.
concentrate/ˈkɑːnsntreɪt/集中/Please concentrate on your studies.
concept/ˈkɑːnsept/概念/The concept of equality is fundamental to democracy.
concern/kənˈsɜːrn/关心；涉及/Environmental protection is a major concern.
conclude/kənˈkluːd/得出结论/The study concluded that exercise improves health.
concrete/ˈkɑːnkriːt/具体的/We need concrete evidence, not just theories.
condemn/kənˈdem/谴责/The government condemned the terrorist attack.
conduct/kənˈdʌkt/进行；行为/The scientist conducted an important experiment.
conference/ˈkɑːnfərəns/会议/An international conference was held in Beijing.
confess/kənˈfes/承认/He confessed to the crime.
confine/kənˈfaɪn/限制/The patient was confined to bed for a week.
confirm/kənˈfɜːrm/确认/Please confirm your attendance by Friday.
conflict/ˈkɑːnflɪkt/冲突/The conflict between the two countries lasted for years.
